  "id": "postalpha-0.75c-3-close-zoom-material-texture",
  "name": "Post-Alpha 0.75C-3 - Close-Zoom Material Texture",
  "status": "implemented_nonbrowser_green_browser_replay_pending",
  "playerPromise": "At close zoom, Atlas buildings read as built from coarse wall and roof material instead of flat color planes.",
  "engineeringPromise": "The renderer adds deterministic wall and roof texture grammar inside the existing vector building path, zoom-gated so overview cameras emit no new material texture commands.",
  "axis": "renderer_close_zoom_material_texture",
  "contract": [
    "Wall material texture draws only when camera zoom is >= 1.55.",
    "Desktop and mobile overview cameras stay below the material texture threshold.",
    "Residential and commerce detail cameras cross the material texture threshold.",
    "Wall material uses wallSurface, wallPoint, and wallQuadPoints only.",
    "Texture variation is seeded from stable building id, face, and course index.",
    "Texture shades derive from bodyColor or roofColor through shadeColor with small deltas.",
    "No Math.random, gradients, filters, shaders, Three.js, bitmaps, textures, dependencies, compiler changes, generator changes, or authored Riverside data changes.",
    "Texture strokes and fills batch into one wall Graphics and one roof Graphics per vector building, not per face or per course."
  ],
